;; fraud/decision.aura
;; Maps a fraud score to a go/no-go decision for the checkout pipeline.
;;
;; The fraud-scoring stage produces a numeric score that represents how
;; risky the current order appears. The pipeline only wants a binary
;; answer from this module: either the order passes and proceeds to
;; commit, or it fails and must be compensated by the saga.
;;
;; Decision rule:
;;   - Scores are non-negative numbers (typically an integer between
;;     0 and 100, but we do not enforce that here).
;;   - If score < threshold: decision is 'PASS (or equivalently #t).
;;   - If score >= threshold: decision is 'FAIL (or equivalently #f).
;;
;; We expose both a fresh threshold getter and a decision function so
;; the orchestrator can read either form. The threshold is a single
;; point of tuning; the rest of the pipeline never sees the raw number.
;;
;; Required exported API:
;;   (api-fraud-decision score) -> 'PASS or 'FAIL
;;   (api-fraud-threshold)      -> numeric threshold

(define api-fraud-threshold
  ;; 50 is the standard "median risk" cut-off; values below it are
  ;; considered safe, values at or above it are rejected.
  50)

(define (api-fraud-decision score)
  (if (< score api-fraud-threshold)
      'PASS
      'FAIL))
